From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: voidforge <voidforge@valuz.io>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:43:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: back/forward lists that survive a relaunch

Plan C20. With "restore windows from previous session" on, a restored tab
gets its back/forward list back, not only its URL.

- -[OACTab sessionHistory] returns the tab's navigation entries (at most
  the renderer's 50, around the current one; the initial blank entry is
  left out) as opaque data: a small versioned envelope (magic, version,
  selected index, count) around //components/sessions'
  SerializedNavigationEntry pickles, the per-entry encoding Chrome's
  session service uses (URL, title, page state with scroll position and
  form contents, referrer, transition, timestamps). nil before the first
  commit and after -close.
- OACTabConfiguration.sessionHistory restores such data into the new
  tab's navigation controller (NavigationController::Restore, then
  LoadIfNecessary, since a hidden tab is not activated) and ignores
  initialURL. Data the bridge cannot read (another version, truncated)
  is ignored and initialURL loads as before.

The shell stores the data per device next to its workspace and never
syncs it.
